# Commit and push after completing work

After completing a bug fix or feature in this repo, create a git commit and push to `origin` (usually `main`) without asking.

## Protocol

1. Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log` in parallel.
2. Stage only relevant files. Never commit secrets or `node_modules`.
3. Write a 1-2 sentence why-focused commit message.
4. Use a PowerShell here-string for the message:

```powershell
git commit -m @"
Message here.

"@
```

5. Do not use `--no-verify`. Do not force-push to `main`. Do not amend already-pushed commits.
6. Push so GitHub Pages can redeploy.
7. Report the commit hash and https://pfaustino.github.io/human-achievements/

Still do not commit if there are no changes.
